# Nexus National Digital Matchmaking Hub — Frontend Master Rule

## 1. Agent mission

Build a polished, fully interactive, frontend-only prototype named **Nexus — National Digital Matchmaking Hub**.

Nexus is a national opportunity-matching ecosystem for Bangladesh that connects:

- Students
- Faculty members
- Universities and university administrators
- Companies, startups, NGOs, research organizations, training providers, scholarship providers, and international partners
- UGC administrators and programme officers
- Helpdesk and dispute-resolution officers

The product must support the complete university-to-career journey. It is not only a job portal. It must cover part-time work, freelancing, skills training, internships, jobs, scholarships, study-abroad opportunities, student projects, project funding, mentoring, faculty exchange, research collaboration, consultancy, technology transfer, UGC co-funding, university approvals, monitoring, helpdesk support, complaints, disputes, analytics, and audit trails.

This prototype has **no backend**. All records are mock data and all workflows are simulated in the browser, but the experience must feel complete and production-like.

## 2. Non-negotiable definition of done

Do not stop after creating a landing page, dashboard shell, static mockup, or partial route skeleton.

The implementation is complete only when:

1. Every route defined in this rule exists.
2. Every important button, menu item, filter, tab, form, modal, drawer, dropdown, status action, pagination control, and CTA performs a visible action.
3. Authentication, registration, onboarding, role switching, applications, approvals, offers, funding, messaging, helpdesk, and dispute flows can be demonstrated end to end with dummy data.
4. Data-changing actions update the interface immediately and persist after refresh through `localStorage`.
5. All pages have responsive mobile, tablet, and desktop layouts.
6. There are no dead links, empty placeholder screens, `TODO` blocks, or “coming soon” labels for features listed in this rule.
7. Empty, loading, success, error, disabled, rejected, expired, and pending states are represented where relevant.
8. `npm run lint` and `npm run build` pass before the task is considered complete.
9. The app clearly displays a subtle global notice that it is a prototype and all data is simulated.

When a requirement is ambiguous, make a sensible product decision and continue. Prefer a complete coherent flow over asking repeated questions.

