## 5.3 Typography

Use a clean sans-serif font. Prefer `Geist` or `Inter` for English and a Bengali-capable fallback such as `Noto Sans Bengali` or `Hind Siliguri` when Bengali text is shown.

Typography hierarchy:

- Hero title: strong but not oversized
- Page title: 28–36 px desktop, 24–30 px mobile
- Section title: 20–24 px
- Card title: 16–18 px
- Body: 14–16 px
- Metadata: 12–14 px

Use readable line lengths and generous vertical rhythm.

## 5.4 Layout rules

- Marketing pages: centered max-width container around 1200–1280 px.
- Portal pages: fixed/collapsible desktop sidebar, top bar, content max width where appropriate.
- Mobile: off-canvas sidebar and bottom-safe spacing.
- Cards: 12–16 px radius, subtle border, very light shadow.
- Forms: clear labels above fields, helper text, inline validation, visible required markers.
- Tables: responsive; switch to card rows on narrow screens when needed.
- Long pages: use sticky section navigation or tabs where useful.

## 5.5 Theme and language

Implement:

- Light mode
- Dark mode
- System theme option
- Persisted theme preference
- English/Bangla language toggle

The core shell, navigation, authentication pages, common actions, status names, empty states, and main dashboard labels should switch language. Long mock opportunity descriptions may remain English, but the language toggle must visibly work and should not be decorative.

## 5.6 Accessibility

Meet strong practical accessibility standards:

- Semantic headings in logical order
- Keyboard navigation for menus, dialogs, tabs, command palette, filters, and forms
- Visible focus rings
- Proper labels and descriptions for inputs
- `aria-label` for icon-only controls
- Focus trapping and Escape handling in modals/drawers
- Sufficient contrast
- Status communication through text and icon, never color alone
- Meaningful alt text for informational images
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Charts must have adjacent text summaries or accessible labels
- No interaction that works only on hover

