# 20. Required end-to-end demo flows

These flows must work across roles using shared persistent state.

## 20.1 Student internship flow

1. Student logs in.
2. Student sees an 88% internship match.
3. Student opens the match explanation.
4. Student applies and uploads mock documents.
5. Application status becomes `University review`.
6. Switch to University Admin.
7. Admin reviews score, schedule, organization, and documents.
8. Admin approves.
9. Switch to Organization.
10. Organization sees candidate in pipeline and shortlists.
11. Organization schedules interview.
12. Student sees interview in notifications and calendar.
13. Organization creates offer.
14. Student accepts.
15. University confirms the match.
16. Internship appears as active and is monitored.

## 20.2 UGC 50/50 co-funded internship flow

1. Organization chooses an eligible internship and candidate.
2. Organization enters total stipend and sets 50% company / 50% UGC.
3. Organization submits co-funding request.
4. University Admin verifies candidate enrollment and opportunity.
5. UGC reviews eligibility and budget.
6. UGC approves with payment milestones.
7. Student finance page shows the split and payment schedule.
8. Organization records company contribution.
9. UGC milestone becomes payable.
10. Payment timeline and audit events update for all relevant roles.

## 20.3 First-year financial-support flow

1. Student uses journey simulator to become first year.
2. Recommendations change to part-time work, free training, tutoring, and need-based support.
3. Student enrolls in a free course.
4. Student completes the course.
5. A new skill becomes verified.
6. Matching scores for relevant part-time work improve.
7. Student applies for an internet or transport support grant.
8. University verifies need.
9. UGC approves a mock amount.

## 20.4 Scholarship/study-abroad flow

1. Student selects destination and degree preference.
2. System shows eligibility matches and gaps.
3. Student adds scholarship to planner.
4. Student completes a document checklist.
5. Student requests a faculty recommendation.
6. Faculty accepts and uploads a placeholder letter.
7. University verifies enrollment/transcript.
8. Student marks external submission complete.
9. Outcome status can be updated to shortlisted/awarded/rejected.

## 20.5 Student project-funding flow

1. Student creates a project and team.
2. Student requests faculty supervision.
3. Faculty accepts.
4. Student submits funding request with milestones and budget.
5. University verifies.
6. UGC approves or requests changes.
7. Student records milestone progress.
8. Funding release status updates.
9. Organization can express interest in the project.

## 20.6 Faculty technology-transfer flow

1. Faculty creates a technology listing.
2. University Admin reviews ownership and IP status.
3. Listing becomes visible in technology marketplace.
4. Organization submits collaboration/licensing interest.
5. Faculty and organization exchange messages.
6. University records review status and next step.

## 20.7 Dispute flow

1. Student reports unpaid stipend linked to an internship.
2. University receives and mediates the dispute.
3. Organization submits a response.
4. University records a decision.
5. Student appeals.
6. UGC receives the escalated case.
7. UGC requests evidence and resolves with a remedy.
8. Payment record, organization risk score, notifications, and audit logs update.

## 20.8 Helpdesk SLA flow

1. User creates a ticket.
2. Helpdesk queue displays SLA countdown.
3. Officer assigns and replies.
4. Ticket is resolved.
5. User rates support.
6. SLA dashboard recalculates the 24-hour resolution rate.

