# 25. Permissions and route behavior

Create a clear permissions map in `src/lib/permissions.js`.

Rules:

- Guests can browse public listings but must log in to save, apply, message, or create records.
- Students can edit only their own profile, applications, projects, tickets, and disputes.
- Faculty can manage their own applications, technologies, research interests, and mentoring.
- Organizations can see only candidate data shared through consent or applications.
- University admins can access users and records connected to their institution.
- UGC can access national aggregate and oversight records.
- Helpdesk officers can access tickets and linked context but not unrestricted private academic data.

Because this is frontend-only, route protection is a UX simulation, not security. Still implement redirects and unauthorized screens so role flows are coherent.

