# 28. Performance and code quality

- Use `next/image` for raster images if any are used.
- Prefer self-contained local placeholder assets; do not depend on remote image services for the core experience.
- Use dynamic import for large chart sections when appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders and giant store selectors.
- Memoize expensive derived lists and match calculations where useful.
- Do not generate random values during render.
- Use stable IDs.
- Keep page and component files reasonably sized.
- Centralize constants and labels.
- Avoid duplicated status strings and route definitions.
- Keep browser console free of warnings and errors.
- Do not expose secrets or require environment variables for the prototype.

