# 30. Implementation sequence

When building the project from scratch, follow this order.

## Phase 1 — Foundation

1. Scaffold the Next.js JavaScript project.
2. Install approved dependencies.
3. Create design tokens and global styles.
4. Create reusable UI primitives.
5. Create layouts, route groups, theme, language support, and prototype banner.
6. Create data models, seed data, store, mock services, permissions, and matching engine.

## Phase 2 — Public site and authentication

1. Build all public routes.
2. Build registration/login/TIGERfed/OTP/password flows.
3. Build onboarding for every role.
4. Verify responsive navigation and guest restrictions.

## Phase 3 — Student portal

Implement every student route and all student-side interactions, then validate the first-year, final-year, scholarship, project, funding, and support flows.

## Phase 4 — Faculty and organization portals

Implement faculty workflows, organization opportunity posting, candidate pipeline, interviews, offers, co-funding, projects, courses, and partnerships.

## Phase 5 — University, UGC, and helpdesk portals

Implement institutional review, national oversight, financial approvals, disputes, risk, audit, analytics, and SLA management.

## Phase 6 — Cross-role integration and QA

1. Verify all required end-to-end flows.
2. Ensure every state mutation appears across relevant roles.
3. Verify persistence after refresh.
4. Fix accessibility and responsive issues.
5. Remove dead code and placeholders.
6. Run lint and production build.
7. Review every route manually.

Do not declare completion at the end of an earlier phase.

